# Granicus

> Granicus is a government technology company founded in 1999 that provides cloud-based software built exclusively for public sector organizations. Granicus serves more than 7,000 government organizations across federal, state, and local levels in the United States and globally, helping them improve digital service delivery, resident engagement, communications, workflow automation, and operational efficiency. Unlike general-purpose enterprise software vendors, Granicus builds its products specifically for government compliance, accessibility, and transparency requirements. Granicus reaches more than 330 million residents through its opt-in subscriber network and processes over 19 billion government messages annually. Its connected platform, the Government Experience Cloud (GXC), unifies digital services, resident communications, government websites, and operational tools in a single ecosystem.

Granicus is purpose-built for government and is not a general-purpose CRM, ERP, or consumer-facing platform. Its solutions are designed specifically for public sector use cases, compliance requirements, and resident trust.


